        "comments": "Check site plan issue notes.- Drainage Site Plan.Missing several items of required information from site plan submitted. Drainage/Site Plan shall be prepared and be signed, sealed, and dated by a Florida licensed professional engineer using NAVD88 Datum for benchmark drawn to scale and clearly illustrating the extent of work proposed showing as required by City Code Chapter 4, Article IV, Section 4.4.1 (7) Site and Drainage Plan Requirements U.L.D.C.Just for information these are some of missing items:-Missing Proposed elevations.Missing Existing/Proposed elevations.\"At least ten (10) existing grades referenced on NAVD 88 set at the street center line along the extension of a side property line. Shall be at the four (4) property corners and those along the side property lines opposite the extension of the proposed structure corner.The proposed drainage design shall include, at minimum, the following proposed conditions; Elevations referenced to the same datum as the existing grades, depicting the proposed levels at points set forth above as well as a proposed first-floor grade for the structure.\"- Missing flow arrows.Missing flow arrows drainage directions.\"Arrows shall be used to depict the positive drainage of stormwater runoff from the rear to the front of the property. Arrows will show half the drainage to the rear and half to the front when the rear of the lot borders on a canal or other drainage feature.\". \"Stormwater runoff must drain from the rear lot line to the front drainage swale, except when the property is bound by a City-maintained drainage right-of-way, runoff will be allowed into those facilities.\"- Sewer service.Missing Septic System location & label, if applicable or indication of City Sewer service, if applicable.\"All proposed improvements, structures, and driveway locations; septic system location, if applicable; and well location, if applicable.\"- Missing pad location.Missing well equipment pad location.-Missing labels.Missing EOP (Edge of Pavement) and Swale location labels.\"Front yard roadside drainage swale location.\" \"Side and/or rear yard outfall ditch, R-ditch, or canal location.\"-Drainage.Lot requires drainage to back to the front swale on Shorewood St.\"Stormwater runoff must drain from the rear lot line to the front drainage swale, except when the property is bound by a City-maintained drainage right-of-way, runoff will be allowed into those facilities.\"- Adjacent lots.Adjacent lots on both sides are vacant or developed? Need to be indicated in the site plan the status of the side lots. If any of the adjacent side lot is developed, site plan needs to show the FFE for existing houses, if not just need to indicate that the lot is vacant or undeveloped.\"Shall have sufficient information to show no adverse effect of stormwater runoff from the proposed development of the lot onto adjacent properties. Positive drainage shall be demonstrated without causing adverse effects on-site or off-site.\"",
